    "title": "Amy Madigan Just Won an Oscar for ‘Weapons’—Here’s Where You Can Stream It",
    "text": "AdvertisementReturn to HomepageTrending: Amazon Big Spring Sale early dealsWhy scalp care is the new skincareOn-sale spring dresses our style editor is obsessed withOrganizing pros: 10 space-saving itemsWhere and When to Stream ‘Weapons’Warner Bros.\"Hearst Magazines and Yahoo may earn commission or revenue on some items through these links.\"It's the movie that made Jordan Peele fire some of his staff after they lost the massive bidding war to make it. And it's also being called the best horror film of 2025. Obviously, we're talking about Weapons, Zach Cregger's big follow-up to Barbarian that will definitely make you second-guess walking back home in the dark. With so many secrets lying in the film, you're definitely not going to want to hesitate in seeing this ASAP—especially because it was up for several Oscars this year, and Amy Madigan took home the trophy for Best Supporting Actress.Here’s everything you need to know about watching Weapons.When did Weapons come out?Weapons was officially released on August 8, 2025 after originally being pushed from its January 2025 release date.Where to watch and stream Weapons Since Weapons is a Warner Bros. film, we already know it’s out on HBO Max. It’s also available to stream on Hulu, so we can watch with the lights on at home!!AdvertisementAdvertisementShop NowShop NowYou Might Also LikeCancel Your Reservation—We Found 35 Delicious Birthday Dinner RecipesMy Legs Couldn't Be Softer, Thanks to This Hair Removal DeviceFound: Top-Rated Dresses on Amazon That Are Actually Worth the BuyView commentsTerms and Privacy PolicyYour Privacy ChoicesAbout Our AdsTerms and Privacy PolicyYour Privacy ChoicesAbout Our AdsAdvertisementRecommended articlesAdvertisementAdvertisement",
